#+TITLE: Intermittent Windows hosted protocol log cleanup failure
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: reproducible-lock-owner
#+BRANCH: master

* Symptom and reproduction
On 2026-10-08, make test failed in
PROTOCOL-REAL-LITERALS-REACH-THE-ENGINE-EXACTLY while deleting
logs/Drawing1_2026-10-08_20-40-06.log in the hosted-rest workdir.
Windows reported that another process was using the file.
Run make -C autolisp-front-end test-sbcl with clautolisp-sbcl built.

* Investigation
The same test passed (12 checks) on the next local Windows SBCL run.
DRIVE-HOSTED-ENGINE waits for the child, then terminates/waits again in
its unwind cleanup before deleting the workdir. The lock owner and
cause remain unknown; a process or external scanner may hold the file.
Capture the locking process and child exit state when this recurs before
choosing a lifecycle fix or a bounded cleanup retry. Do not suppress
cleanup errors or assume this is fixed by the quit-only argv correction.

* Additional SCHMS evidence -- 2026-10-27 (installed ALFE 2.3.23)

[[https://fabrik.sncf.fr/gitlab/dmoe-pop/epure/es/schms/-/jobs/554713][AutoCAD ActiveX job 554713]]
expired in BOOTSTRAP after 120 seconds with status BOOTING. Following jobs
554714 and 554715 failed BEFORE checkout because the drawing log remained
locked. Earlier in this qualification, a concrete owner was identified:
acad.exe /Automation -Embedding, runner0, created at 12:59:20 UTC. Its drawing
log contained the load of SCHMS test-cad-activex's run-common.lsp. That instance
was still alive when diagnosed at 14:37 UTC; it was closed only after verifying
its identity, creation time, owner and the completed-test log. Other projects'
active CAD instances were preserved. The log then opened exclusively.

A separate operational fault was also found and removed: two gitlab-runner
supervisors used the SAME runner0 configuration. Do not conflate that with the
COM lifecycle issue. A per-configuration OS lock now prevents that duplication
(run-forest-run MR !5).

The installed Windows bridge is old (2.3.23). Current master already contains
created-PID and COM quit work; verify this failure path on the current Windows
build before choosing a further source fix or closing this ticket. The observed
2.3.23 timeout must not leave an invisible COM server holding the checkout.
SCHMS's pure ActiveX suite now uses its native GUI launcher with an explicit
clean profile and the same assertions, avoiding the old bridge for this lane.
This is a qualification workaround, not proof that ALFE's current lifecycle is
fixed. No failed assertion is suppressed.
